# An empty cell is an unknown rather than a no, and `and` and `or` read it
# that way: one that cannot change the answer does not decide it. So a check
# still waiting leaves a decision empty, except where the other check has
# already settled it. Write `a // false` to read a gap as a no instead.

sheet Applications

Score : Int
Refs  : Int

| Name | Score | Refs | Passed | Enough | Decided | Rejected | Settled |
| ---- | ----- | ---- | ------ | ------ | ------- | -------- | ------- |
| Ada  | 72    | 2    | *      | *      | *       | *        | *       |
| Brin | 41    |      | *      | *      | *       | *        | *       |
| Cho  |       | 1    | *      | *      | *       | *        | *       |
| Dara | 88    |      | *      | *      | *       | *        | *       |
| Eze  |       |      | *      | *      | *       | *        | *       |

Passed   := Score >= 60
Enough   := Refs >= 2
Decided  := Passed and Enough
Rejected := not Passed or not Enough
Settled  := (Passed // false) and (Enough // false)
